    "lawCode": "Add §443-b, amd §441-c, RP L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10274\n\nSPONSOR: FERNANDEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property law, in relation to access to fair and\ntransparent real estate listings\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRequires timely public advertising or marketing of listed residential\nproperties on platfo accessible to the general public; permits non-publ-\nic marketing only where the seller gives informed, written direction\nafter receiving a standardized state disclosure that clearly explains\nthe risks and tradeoffs of withholding a listing from public marketing.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Short title.\n\nSection 2: Legislative findings and intent.\n\nSection 3: Amends real property law by adding a new section 443-b,\n\"Marketing\". Defines \"publicly advertise or market\", \"Private or limited\naccess channels\", \"Licensee\", and \"Multiple listing service\".  Outlines\nresponsibilities of a seller or landlord under this legislation,\nprovides opt-out form.\n\nSection 4: Penalties and provisions.\n\nSection 5: Enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAccess to information shapes outcomes for buyers and sellers. Private\nListing Networks are a strategy real estate brokers use to quietly shop\ntheir properties to internal audiences for indefinite periods of time,\nout of sight from other brokerages and a global pool of potentially\nwilling buyers. Often, this is followed by a subsequent \"Coming Soon\"\nphase where properties are marketed on select public portals without key\ninsights like days on market or price adjustments. If this phase also\nproduces no buyers, then the property is listed on the MLS for all\nagents and buyers to see. But even though the property has been listed\non various private markets for a given time, from the buyer's perspec-\ntive the property has just hit \"the market\".\n\nThis legislation requires that listings posted on any market must also\nbe listed on public access channels. Sellers or landlords are given the\noption to opt out after signing a disclosure provided in this bill which\nacknowledges the potential consequences of withholding their property\nfrom public marketing.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall have become a law. Effective immediately, the addition, amendment\nand/or repeal of any rule or regulation necessary for the implementation\nof this act on its effective date are authorized to be made and\ncompleted on or before such effective date.\n",
